---@field isHttpsAllowed? boolean Indicates whether HTTPS traffic is allowed on the endpoint. Default value is true. At least one protocol (HTTP or HTTPS) must be allowed.
---@field queryStringCachingBehavior? azure.cdn.EndpointPropertiesUpdateParametersQueryStringCachingBehavior|string Defines how CDN caches requests that include query strings. You can ignore any query strings when caching, bypass caching to prevent requests that contain query strings from being cached, or cache every request with a unique URL.
---@field optimizationType? azure.cdn.OptimizationType|string Specifies what scenario the customer wants this CDN endpoint to optimize for, e.g. Download, Media services. With this information, CDN can apply scenario driven optimization.
---@field probePath? string Path to a file hosted on the origin which helps accelerate delivery of the dynamic content and calculate the most optimal routes for the CDN. This is relative to the origin path. This property is only relevant when using a single origin.
---@field geoFilters? azure.cdn.EndpointPropertiesUpdateParametersGeoFiltersList List of rules defining the user's geo access within a CDN endpoint. Each geo filter defines an access rule to a specified path or content, e.g. block APAC for path /pictures/
